{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgS5GsC3czNNPduPkVxPx","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"launchd has been running the job every night (6 runs, last exit code 1), but two bugs stacked so nothing ever reached you. I've fixed both scripts. Auth will still fail until you add a token on your Mac (see below).\n\n**Causes** (written up in `ANSWER.md`):\n1. **`claude` isn't logged in when launchd runs it.** The error log says `Not logged in · Please run /login`. launchd doesn't load `~/.zshrc` or `~/.zprofile`, so whatever login works in your terminal isn't available to the job. `claude -p` exits 1 straight away.\n2. **The failure note could never be sent.** In zsh, `status` is a built-in read-only variable, so `status=$?` on line 19 is a fatal error. The script stopped there and neither `notify.sh` call ran. I reproduced this: `zsh -c 'true; status=$?; echo after'` never prints \"after\".\n\n**Fixes:**\n- **`bin/nightly-review.zsh`:**\n  - `status` is renamed to `rc`.\n  - The script loads secrets from `~/.config/nightly-review.env` if that file exists.\n  - `claude`'s error output is saved and included in the failure message, so you'd have gotten \"Not logged in\" on Telegram.\n  - Timestamped log lines go to the launchd error log, and a failed `notify.sh` is logged.\n  - Read-only tools (file reading and `git log/show/diff`) are pre-approved, because headless mode can't ask for permission and would refuse `git log`.\n  - The 3-line summary now comes first in the output and is what gets sent. Before, the script sent the first 300 characters while asking for the summary at the end.\n- **`bin/notify.sh`:** curl now fails when Telegram returns an error and logs the reply. Before, a bad token or chat ID still exited 0 and the reply was thrown away.\n\nI checked both scripts for syntax and ran the job against stand-ins for `claude` and `notify.sh`. A \"Not logged in\" failure now sends a failure message, and a successful run sends the summary. The real `claude` and Telegram weren't called.\n\n**What you need to do on your Mac:**\n1. Run `claude setup-token`.\n2. Put `export CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN=<token>` in `~/.config/nightly-review.env` and run `chmod 600` on it.\n3. Test the way launchd runs it: `launchctl kickstart -k gui/$UID/com.vk.nightly-review`.\n\nThe plist itself is fine and doesn't need reloading."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1574,"cache_read_input_tokens":28007,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1574},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e6272efd-1b6f-4b7b-9d76-84a5acf665ca","uuid":"9ace43c9-508f-4784-bf29-7040e6a24577","timestamp":"2026-10-27T04:00:54.963Z","request_id":"req_011CgS5GrjWxnhL1NESi6ygb"}
